From c8acfbc07d593d3e904ac7e56d7b61a1bec328fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: japabu <japa.busse@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:28:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dma_reach: an investigation probe of the address bits each
 HDA function carries

Not for landing. The AMD bench's HDMI audio function 03:00.1 faulted at its
ring addresses with bit 46 dropped. This probe measures, on a boot armed
`claim-floor=40000000` so a claim's grants sit below 4 GiB, which bits of a
device address each HD Audio function carries to the unit: its upper base
registers' read-back, the codec link and an output stream at the grant, the
same aimed with one bit above it set from 63 down until one reaches nothing,
and two patterns over bits 32 to 47. The unit's DMA FAULT records name the
address each failing step issued.

`claim-floor=` is a test-kernel valued actuator; `dma_reach_qemu_smoke`
checked the protocol on QEMU's ich9-intel-hda behind VT-d.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
